Load web tools with ToolSearch "select:WebSearch,WebFetch". Do not edit any file.

CANDIDATES (JSON):
${JSON.stringify(batch)}`

const verdictSets = (await parallel(batches.map((b, i) => () =>
  agent(verifyPrompt(b, i), { label: `verify:batch-${i + 1}`, phase: 'Verify', schema: VERIFY_SCHEMA })
))).filter(Boolean)
const verdicts = verdictSets.flatMap(v => v.verdicts || [])
const unverified = merged.candidates.filter(c => !verdicts.find(v => v.id === c.id)).map(c => c.id)
if (unverified.length) log(`unverified candidates: ${unverified.join(', ')}`)

// ---------- Phase 5: synthesize ----------
phase('Synthesize')

const final = await agent(`${CONTEXT}

You write the panel's final answer. You have: the Frame Job inventory, four research sweeps, three strategists' proposals, the merged candidates, and adversarial verdicts on each (already-have checks against the code, feasibility, and a market refutation attempt). Unverified candidate ids, if any: ${JSON.stringify(unverified)}.

Produce:
- thesis: two or three sentences — what single idea would make Frame Job a leading editor for creators, given what it uniquely has.
- top_bets: the 4-6 bets that matter most, ranked, each with a concrete pitch (what the creator does and sees), why it puts Frame Job ahead (not just level), what existing Frame Job work it builds on, effort (S/M/L/XL as build effort, never lines of code), and risks. Drop or demote anything a verifier marked already shipped or whose market case collapsed; if you keep one a verifier doubted, say why.
- also_worth_doing: the next tier, briefly.
- not_worth_chasing: what the evidence says not to chase, with reasons.
- owner_decisions: the decisions only the owner can make before any of this is built (e.g. which non-goals to lift, whether any cloud service is acceptable beyond BYO key, which creator segment to lead with).
- report_md: a complete Markdown survey document for the repo at designs/creator-survey.md. Structure: title "# Creator survey: what would make Frame Job a leading creator editor"; a one-paragraph summary dated 2026-11-01; "## What Frame Job has" (brief, from the inventory, including what was checked absent); "## The market in late 2026" (per segment: creator tools, pro editors, screen/tutorial tools, what creators ask for — with the tools' headline features and status); "## The bets" (the ranked top bets in full, then the next tier); "## Not worth chasing"; "## Decisions for the owner"; "## Sources" (every URL used for a claim, grouped by section, with as-of dates). Write in plain, precise prose: short declarative sentences, no marketing words, no emoji, British/plain spelling is fine. Every market claim in the body carries a source in the Sources section. Mark shipped vs beta vs announced. Do not invent sources; use only URLs present in the evidence.
Do not edit any file.

EVIDENCE (JSON):
${JSON.stringify({ inventory, research, strategies, merged, verdicts })}`, { label: 'synthesize:final', phase: 'Synthesize', schema: FINAL_SCHEMA })

return { final, merged, verdicts, strategies, inventory, research }

