The guide is written. It's at `~/devel/framejob/.claude/worktrees/creator-jobs/tools/proof/media/creator/RECORDING-GUIDE.md`, which is gitignored and sits in the same folder your recordings go into.

It covers:
- **Before you start:** build once with `make app` and use that build all day. Give Frame Job the four permissions. Input Monitoring has to be added by hand with **+**, because macOS shows no prompt.
- **1. Talking head (S-TH1, about 6 minutes):**
  - the camera and sound setup, with the RØDE as its own file and a clap at the start;
  - the script of moments: a clean first minute, retakes, false starts, a pause, and the timed physical moments;
  - the CP1 cut, done only through the Transcript tab, with what to note and the JOB-11 listening check.
- **2. Screen tutorial (CU12, 10–20 minutes):**
  - a table of the exact recorder settings: Cursor Separate, Record shortcuts on, camera beside, and the When it lands boxes;
  - what to do while recording;
  - cutting it with the new tools, including the JOB-25 Auto Zoom check;
  - what to time and note, with an optional hand-cut comparison.
- **3. Optional extras while the camera's set up (about 10 minutes):**
  - the V-Log, Apple Log and iPhone HDR clips;
  - the hard cutout cases;
  - the plain-cloth clip;
  - an In the picture tutorial;
  - a window-drag recording.

  Each one pays off checks that are already owed.

The talking head is the one that matters most. It unblocks TX4–TX7, Find Clips and multi-track audio.

